[ledge] These are the three annular M3 head-bearing shoulders at Z=-0.8 mm inside the 6.15 mm counterbores. They hold recessed screw heads behind the gasket and underneath the locating pedestals. The 3.075 mm radial opening is accessible from the underside before the gasket is installed; retain Bambu automatic supports as selected for an actual print and inspect these seats after cleanup.
alternatives: A sloped bearing does not seat a flat screw head. Omitting the recess puts heads into the gasket/countertop interface. A wider recess reduces the bearing annulus and surrounding plate stock.
